    "field": "Sports / Exercise Physiology",
    "plotType": "Line plot (muscle force vs. contraction velocity, hyperbolic)",
    "description": "The force–velocity curve plots the force a muscle can produce against the velocity at which it shortens, tracing the classic inverse hyperbolic relationship first described by A.V. Hill: the faster a muscle contracts, the less force it can generate, and maximal force occurs only when velocity is near zero. In whole-athlete testing the same relationship is measured across loaded jumps or sprints to profile an athlete's strength–speed balance. Coaches use it to decide whether an athlete needs to develop more maximal strength or more speed.",
