    "whatItTellsYou": "Where the curve sits and how it is shaped shows the athlete's profile: a curve biased toward the high-force/low-velocity end means a strength-dominant athlete, while one biased toward high-velocity/low-force means a speed-dominant athlete. The theoretical maximal force and maximal velocity intercepts quantify the two ends and reveal which quality to train.",
