    "id": "sport-hr-recovery",
    "title": "Heart-Rate Recovery Curve",
    "field": "Sports / Exercise Physiology",
    "plotType": "Time-series decay curve (heart rate vs. time post-exercise)",
    "description": "The heart-rate recovery curve tracks how quickly heart rate falls after exercise stops, decaying from the peak toward resting as the parasympathetic nervous system reasserts control. The rate of the initial drop — often summarized as the beats recovered in the first 60 seconds — is a window into autonomic health and cardiovascular fitness. Physiologists and clinicians use it because a fast recovery reflects good vagal reactivation and is a recognized marker of both fitness and cardiac risk.",
