    "whatItTellsYou": "A steep, rapid decline in the first minute indicates strong parasympathetic reactivation and good cardiovascular fitness; a shallow, slow decline indicates blunted autonomic recovery and is associated with lower fitness and elevated cardiac risk. Improvement in recovery speed over a training program signals rising fitness.",
