    "id": "sport-wingate-power",
    "title": "Wingate Anaerobic Power Profile",
    "field": "Sports / Exercise Physiology",
    "plotType": "Time-series power curve (power output over a 30-s all-out sprint)",
    "description": "The Wingate power profile plots mechanical power output second-by-second across a 30-second all-out cycling sprint against resistance, capturing the signature of anaerobic energy delivery. Power spikes to a peak within the first few seconds, then declines as the anaerobic stores deplete, ending at a lower value that defines the athlete's fatigue. It is the classic laboratory test for characterizing anaerobic power and capacity in sprinters and power athletes.",
    "dataNeeded": [
      {
        "name": "Time",
        "unit": "s"
      },
      {
        "name": "Power output",
        "unit": "W·kg⁻¹"
      }
    ],
    "whatItTellsYou": "The early peak power indexes explosive anaerobic capability, the average power over 30 s indexes anaerobic capacity, and the fatigue index (the drop from peak to lowest power) indexes how fast the athlete tires. A high peak with a steep decline marks a fast-twitch, sprint-type profile; a lower peak that is better maintained marks greater fatigue resistance.",
